// FOLLOWER MON - overworld companion Pokemon (v0 / first pass)
// ================================================================================================
// GOAL (from the project owner): "a fully effective Follower pokemon like in HeartGold and SoulSilver".
//
// WHY THIS ISN'T A PORT OF HGSS'S FOLLOWER: HGSS's follower is a 3D model (NSBMD), reusing HGSS's own
// fully-3D overworld character engine and a dedicated library of ~500 species x form x gender 3D models
// (see the sibling PokeHeartGold project's src/follow_mon.c). Platinum's overworld is entirely 2D-sprite
// based - it ships NO 3D Pokemon models and no per-species 2D "walking" sprite sheets for the roster at
// large (confirmed: no .nsbmd Pokemon assets anywhere in this repo, and res/pokemon/<species>/ only has
// battle sprites, an icon, and a footprint - none of which are pre-formatted as a 4-directional overworld
// character sprite). A literal port is not possible without either new 3D engine work or hand-drawn
// overworld sprites for ~493 species, neither of which is something this assistant can produce.
//
// WHAT PLATINUM ALREADY HAS, INSTEAD: Amity Square (the real DPPt/Platinum "walk with your Pokemon" area)
// and several partner-trainer dungeon sequences (Cheryl/Riley/Marley/Buck/Mira, and the rival on Route 201)
// already use a fully-built, already-shipped, already-tested "an object trails the player's movement"
// system: MOVEMENT_TYPE_FOLLOW_PLAYER (generated/movement_types.h). Once a MapObject has this movement
// type, Platinum's own (undecompiled-in-detail, but working) engine code handles 100% of the actual
// step-by-step trailing behavior - this file does NOT implement any movement/pathing logic itself, the
// same way it doesn't need to. Amity Square also proves out a genuine species -> overworld-graphic mapping,
// but only for a curated whitelist of ~19 species that have dedicated pre-built 2D sprite resources
// (generated/object_events_gfx.h's OBJ_EVENT_GFX_<SPECIES> entries) - there is currently no way to display
// species outside that list without new art assets, so FOLLOWER_GRAPHICS_TABLE below is intentionally the
// SAME whitelist Amity Square already uses (Pikachu, Clefairy, Jigglypuff, Psyduck, Torchic, Skitty,
// Drifloon, Pachirisu, Shroomish, Buneary, Happiny, the Turtwig/Chimchar/Piplup lines).
//
// WHAT THIS ADDS ON TOP OF AMITY SQUARE'S OWN (vanilla) BEHAVIOR:
//   1. Availability everywhere, not just inside one map - hooked into FieldMapChange_CreateObjects/
//      _LoadObjects (src/field_map_change.c), the same place the player's own avatar object is created on
//      every map load, instead of a single map's own script.
//   2. Tied to the REAL current party leader (first non-egg, non-fainted party Pokemon), not a
//      player-chosen "pick one Pokemon to walk with today" menu selection.
//   3. Dynamically created via MapObjectMan_AddMapObject (no per-map static object-event data needed,
//      unlike Amity Square's LOCALID_FOLLOWER_MON, which only exists because that ONE map's data defines
//      it) - so no map data files needed editing for this to work on every map.
//
// KNOWN LIMITATIONS OF THIS v0 (disclosed, not fixed here):
//   - Species outside the ~19-species whitelist: no visible follower (silently not spawned - see
//     FollowerMon_GetGraphicsID). Extending this to the full roster would need a genuinely new rendering
//     path (e.g. adapting src/overlay006/hm_cut_in.c's CharacterSprite_LoadPokemonSprite technique, which
//     loads a Pokemon's raw battle-sprite tiles at runtime, into a persistent walking object) - substantial
//     additional engineering, not attempted in this pass.
//   - COLOR ROTATION (ENTRY P13) and MID-MAP LEADER-CHANGE SYNC (this entry) are now both handled -
//     FollowerMon_Refresh updates the existing object's graphics in place (rather than delete+recreate)
//     when the leader's species changes, and FollowerMon_RefreshPalette re-applies the rotated palette -
//     both called every field frame from FieldMap_Main (src/overlay005/fieldmap.c), so neither needs a
//     dedicated call site at every possible "party changed" event (menu reorder, faint, evolve, trade,
//     catch, etc.) - any of them self-correct within one frame.
//   - Not tested in-game (no emulator/hardware available to this assistant) - unlike everything else in
//     this project, there is no prior art in EITHER sibling project to directly verify this against, since
//     even PokeHeartGold's follower is a fundamentally different (3D) implementation. This is the single
//     highest-risk, least-verified piece of this entire port; treat it accordingly.
typedef struct FollowerGraphicsEntry {
    u16 species;
    u16 graphicsID;
} FollowerGraphicsEntry;

